d%20by%20CSSWG%20Resolution","name":"Closed Accepted by CSSWG Resolution","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes backed by a CSSWG resolution.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":469426704,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0Njk0MjY3MDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Needs%20Edits","name":"Needs Edits","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":741667480,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3NDE2Njc0ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-break-4","name":"css-break-4","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/milestones/15","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/milestone/15","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/milestones/15/labels","id":5955303,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNTk1NTMwMw==","number":15,"title":"TPAC-2020-08-23","description":"","creator":{"login":"astearns","id":1380751,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODA3NTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1380751?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns","html_url":"https://github.com/astearns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astearns/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5,"closed_issues":8,"state":"closed","created_at":"2020-10-05T22:44:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-26T21:46:57Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2021-02-02T01:06:44Z"},"comments":8,"created_at":"2018-12-06T16:51:39Z","updated_at":"2020-10-23T16:16:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\"Some content is not fragmentable, for example many types of replaced elements [CSS21] (such as images\"\r\nfrom https://drafts.csswg.org/css-break-4/#end-block (actually slightly below that ID)\r\n\r\nWe have always considered replaced elements as monolithic, until there was customer demand for optionally breaking inside images.\r\n\r\nSo we implemented the property `object-slice`, effective on block-level replaced elements (for simplicity from now on called \"images\"):\r\nhttps://www.pdfreactor.com/product/doc_html/index.html#css-property-ro-object-slice\r\n\r\nThe initial value `none` keeps the previous behavior, i.e. monolithic.\r\n`auto` and `avoid` allow fragmentation of the image, `avoid` preferring to move it entirely to the next fragment container if it fits there.\r\n(To avoid overflow and loss of information `avoid` could also be considered as initial value. Large block-level replaced-elements should be rare enough for this to have very little impact on existing documents.)\r\nPlease note that we are only talking block-direction breaks. Handling inline-direction overflow of images is not part of the scope of this property.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, to avoid splitting off small parts at the beginning or end of the image, and to be more in line with blocks containing inline content, we also added support for the `orphans` and `widows` properties. Their values are just multiplied with the used `line-height` of the image box and cause breaks to be avoided or happen earlier, as in text.\r\n\r\nI would like to put the property and related behavior up for discussion and consideration, to give authors (of documents, or of print style sheets) the needed control over large images.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3404/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3404/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}